<table summary="SWI Options_OpenFile">

<tr><th colspan=3 align=left>On entry</th></tr>

 <tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td valign=top width="60">R0&nbsp;=</td><td>Flags :
              <ul><!-- indent -->

<table summary="Table of bits">
<tr><th align=left>Bit</th><th align=left>Meaning if set</th></tr>

               <tr><td valign=top>0-1</td><td>Method of accessing file
                <ul><!-- indent -->

<table summary="Table of values">
<tr><th align=left>Value</th><th align=left>Meaning</th></tr>

                <tr><td valign=top>0</td><td>R1 contains absolute filename</td></tr>
                <tr><td valign=top>1</td><td>R1 contains the leaf name<br>
                                R2 contains the application name,<br>
                                R3 contains another directory name to use
                                if Choices not present, or Choices file not
                                present.</td></tr>
                <tr><td valign=top>2-3</td><td>Reserved</td></tr>
                </table>
</ul><!-- end indent -->
               </td></tr>
               <tr><td valign=top>2-31</td><td>Reserved, must be 0</td></tr>
              </table>
</ul><!-- end indent -->
              </td></tr>
 <tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td valign=top width="60">R1&nbsp;=</td><td>Pointer to filename, or leafname</td></tr>
 <tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td valign=top width="60">R2&nbsp;=</td><td>Pointer to application name</td></tr>
 <tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td valign=top width="60">R3&nbsp;=</td><td>Pointer to directory to use</td></tr>

<tr><th colspan=3 align=left>On exit</th></tr>

 <tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td valign=top width="60">R0&nbsp;=</td><td>Opaque options handle</td></tr>


<tr><th colspan=3 align=left>Use</th></tr>
<tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td colspan=2>
This SWI is used to open a specific, or Choices: file for access. When
opening a specific file (type=0), only that file will be written to and read
from.

<p>When opening a Choices: file (type=1), the file read will come from
<code>Choices:&lt;application&gt;.&lt;leafname&gt;</code> if that is present,
or if not, from <code>&lt;directory&gt;.&lt;leafname&gt;</code>. This
provides compatibility for applications written for older systems. When
writing, data will be written to
<code>&lt;Choices$Write&gt;.&lt;application&gt;.&lt;leafname&gt;</code>
unless the Choices: structure is not present, in which case it will be
written to <code>&lt;directory&gt;.&lt;leafname&gt;</code>.
</td></tr>
</table>

