<table width="100%" border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=1 summary=name>
 <tr bgcolor="#dddddd">
  <td align=centre>
   <h3 align=center><a name="formats"></a>Data formats</h3>
  </td>
 </tr>
</table>

<P>The options files are standard RISC OS text files. Any whitespace (space
or tab) at the beginning or end of a line will be ignored. Any line where the
first non-whitespace character is '#' is a comment line and will be ignored
as will any lines consisting of only whitespace.

<P>The file consists of a series of groups delimited by group name
specifiers. A group name specifier starts with '[' followed by the name,
which may contain spaces, followed by ']'.

<P>The groups themselves are in one of two format (although further formats
may be added in future). The first format (list format) is a simple list of
newline terminated strings.

<p>The second, more complex format consists of tag, value pairs in the
format:

<P><code>&lt;spaces&gt;tag name&lt;spaces&gt;:&lt;spaces&gt;value&lt;spaces&gt;\n</code>
<P>Where <code>&lt;spaces&gt;</code> is 0 or more spaces or tabs.
<P>An example options file would be:
<pre>
# choices file for widget

[auto load]
# a list of files to load when starting widget
ADFS::4.$.afile
ADFS::4.$.somedir.anotherfile
ADFS::4.$.thingy

[misc options]
somevalue    : 42
window width : 332
auto open    : Yes
</pre>

<p>Items at the start of a file (before any group is declared) are deemed to
be in the group $. Group names are case insensitive. Tag entries are case
insensitive.

